  "seoBody": "<p>An engineer is anyone in the field answering workflows on WhatsApp. They don't need an app, a login, or a laptop, just a phone with WhatsApp.</p><h2>Adding</h2><ol><li>Click <strong>+ Add engineer</strong> on the dashboard.</li><li>Enter their name and mobile number (defaults to UK +44; use the picker for other countries).</li><li>Click <strong>Add</strong>. They receive a WhatsApp intro message.</li></ol><h2>What the engineer sees</h2><p>A normal WhatsApp chat. When you send a workflow, they get something like:</p><p><strong>Quickler</strong><br>Hi Tom, Acme Gas has asked you to run the <em>Annual Safety Check</em> at 14 Station Road. Ready to start? Reply YES when you're on site.</p><p>Questions arrive one at a time. The engineer replies with text, numbers, photos, or voice notes. When finished, the report is generated and emailed to you.</p><h2>Removing</h2><p>Click the cross next to their name. Active runs finish but no new ones can be sent. Historical data is kept so reports remain complete.</p><h2>Seats</h2><p>Each plan caps active engineers. The dashboard shows seats remaining. To add more, upgrade your plan.</p><p>Still stuck? Email <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a>, we reply within one business day.</p>",
